    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75348" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρροπύγιον</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῡ]</span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρσοπύγιον</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>GDI</u>
			5702.35
		</span></i> (Samos, <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>), τό:
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρρος</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rump</i> of birds, in which the tail-feathers
			are set, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				504a32
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				618b33
			</span></i>, al. (with vv. ll. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐροπ-,
			ὀροπ-,</span> cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὐροπ-</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				2.189
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρροπ-</span> is certain in <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1498.27
			</span></i> (Athens, <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>)); of the sepia, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				525a12
			</span></i> : generally, <i>tail, rump</i> of any animal, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				1075
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Nu.</u>
				162
			</span></i>.</div>
